If you're building a web application or need programmatic conversion, JavaScript libraries offer the most flexibility. The most popular options are marked, markdown-it, and remark.

Using marked (simplest):
```javascript
import { marked } from 'marked';

const markdown = '# Hello World\n\nThis is **bold** text.';
const html = marked.parse(markdown);
console.log(html);
```

Using markdown-it (most features):
```javascript
import MarkdownIt from 'markdown-it';

const md = new MarkdownIt();
const html = md.render('# Hello World');
```

These libraries run in both Node.js and browsers, making them ideal for server-side rendering, static site generators, and client-side preview features.
